en we looked at active  cast phase eight  and our control t cells shown here in  the black we see that there's up  regulated caspase-8  indicating fast pathway activation this  is compared to  fast deficient t cells shown in the gray  but when we looked at our fast form bbt  cells we see reduce active caspase eight  similar to those in the fast efficient t  cells suggesting that we  are providing a decoy mechanism and  these t cells are experiencing  what reduced fast pathway signaling  so we found that fast form bb improved  the function of the t  cells in vitro but how are we altering  t cell programming  as i mentioned at the beginning of this  talk we know that there are several  metabolic barriers to anti-tumor  immunity  so there's limited nutrients in the  environment as they're being  used by the tumor cells and also t cells  have been shown to have  reduced number of mitochondria as they  are  exposed to the inhibitory to a  microenvironment  several studies have shown that  increased foreign bb singing can  overcome some of these obstacles and  improve metabolism  so form bb stimulated t cells exhibit  higher spare respiratory capacity  which is the reserve energy store for  cells  and this has been linked to long-term  persistence of memory cells  so in these two papers on the left shown  with form bb  card t cells and on the right shown with  1 db agonism via an antibody  we see that there's increased spare  respiratory capacity for the t cells  that have increased volume db signaling  we saw similar results with our fast  form dbt cells  and that they exhibit higher spare  respiratory capacity which was similar  to those publications i just showed you  and also when we looked by microscopy at  the number of mitochondria  we saw increased mitochondrial  biogenesis in the t cells that expressed  fast form bb  relative to our control t cells so they  are generating increasing  numbers of mitochondria and they have  increased metabolism  um pre similar to p